    "@type": "Question",
    "name": "Is Your Small Addition Framing Project Truly Ready to Start?",
    "text": "Is Your Small Addition Framing Project Truly Ready to Start?",
    "answerCount": 1,
    "acceptedAnswer": {
      "@type": "Answer",
      "text": "Thinking about adding a room to your home? That's exciting! But before you grab the hammer, let's make sure your small addition framing project is truly ready to kick off. A big part of this readiness is understanding the timeline and what permits you’ll need. For instance, just getting the permits and approvals can take anywhere from 2 to 10+ weeks depending on your municipality – that’s a pretty wide range, right? A common mistake folks make is underestimating this lag, which can push back your start date significantly. You also want to finalize your scope and drawings, making sure everything is detailed and clear. Another crucial step is procuring your materials, especially standard lumber and sheet goods. If you don’t order these early enough, you could face delays. Small additions often involve rough carpentry and structural coordination, and tying the new framing into your existing house needs to be done correctly. When the addition changes your home's structure, roof lines, or load-bearing walls, or if you need help with permit-ready plans, bringing in experienced framing contractors and design professionals is really important to avoid failed inspections and ensure everything is connected safely. We can help you get organized before you even start digging!",
      "author": {
        "@type": "Organization",
        "name": "HH Remodeling LLC"
      }
    }
  },
